33,2,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,,status,Asuka,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"It seems we have a significant barrier for newcomers. Many potential members are hesitant to commit to a full year's fee upfront, and mid-year joiners require tedious manual calculations.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears the administrative side is quite a beast. I've discovered that chasing small, session-based payments is an absolute time sink compared to a simple yearly collection. We must be careful not to burn out our next treasurer.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The attendance is quite uneven. A small group of people are attending most sessions and handling all the setup and locking up, while some members haven't shown up at all.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's fascinating how a little bit of friction can kill the mood. It seems people have stopped treating our evenings as their own, and some are now overthinking whether it's ""worth it"" to show up.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"The money is tighter than we think. Most of our costs are fixed regardless of turnout, and a third of the members are struggling to pay their renewals on time. We can't just guess the fee.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Benjamin, while I understand the treasurer's burden, we can't ignore that our current system is actively discouraging new people from joining. We are losing potential members over a payment structure.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"A fair point, Asuka. However, we must ask ourselves if we are solving one problem by creating another. If we make joining effortless but the bookkeeping impossible, we'll simply be recruiting new members for a club with no treasurer.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Benjamin, I agree that we must protect the treasurer. However, it is difficult to ignore that a handful of people are carrying the entire weight of the club's physical operations while others pay the same.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Jonathan, it's a classic tragedy. We have the ""dedicated few"" and the ""occasional guests,"" but the real issue is that the guests are now treating the club like a paid service rather than a community.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Jonathan, it doesn't matter who is doing the work if we run out of money. We have huge fixed costs for the hall and insurance that we have to pay no matter what.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, fixed costs are a reality, but if we make the entry fee too high or rigid, we'll have fewer people to share those costs. We need a balance that welcomes newcomers without bankrupting us.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Asuka, a balance is indeed the goal. However, if we introduce a complex, tiered system to accommodate everyone, we might find the treasurer spending more time on spreadsheets than the members spend at the club.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"Perhaps we could find a middle ground. If we can simplify the payment process while acknowledging the disparity in contribution, we might restore some of the inner peace within the group.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Inner peace is a lovely sentiment, Jonathan, but we're dealing with a psychological shift. If we make the fee a hurdle, people will keep weighing the ""value"" of a night out instead of just showing up.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"Stop talking about ""feelings"" and ""inner peace."" We have people who can't even pay their renewals on time. If we don't set a realistic, firm figure based on those fixed costs, the club is finished.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Takumi, being firm is necessary, but being rigid is dangerous. If we ignore the barrier for newcomers, we're just managing the decline of the club. We need a structure that is both fiscally sound and accessible.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It is a delicate dance, isn't it? We are attempting to balance the books, the members' feelings, and the treasurer's sanity. I suspect any ""accessible"" system that involves frequent small payments will be a nightmare to manage.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I believe we should avoid any system that increases the treasurer's workload, but we cannot ignore the resentment building among those who do all the work. A simple, fair solution is necessary for everyone's peace of mind.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Let's be honest: we're trying to solve a cultural problem with a calculator. If we make the fee a transaction, we've already lost. We need a structure that makes belonging feel automatic again.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Takumi,,"Automatic belonging doesn't pay the insurance! We have a real deficit risk here. If we don't prioritize a stable, predictable income that covers those fixed costs, there won't be a club to belong to.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Takumi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
